[bool, np.int8, np.int16, np.int32, np.int64, np.uint8, np.float16, np.float32, np.float64, np.complex64, np.complex128, str, np.dtype]

String value should be selected from the following list:
["ii", "ii->i", "i,j->ij", "bij,bjk->bik", "...ij->...ji", "bn,anm,bm->ba", "none", "mean", "sum", "max", "constant", "tanh"]

[API Documentation]
Applies local response normalization over an input signal.

    The input signal is composed of several input planes, where channels occupy the second dimension.
    Applies normalization across channels.

    .. math::
        b_{c} = a_{c}\left(k + \frac{\alpha}{n}
        \sum_{c'=\max(0, c-n/2)}^{\min(N-1,c+n/2)}a_{c'}^2\right)^{-\beta}

    Args:
        size: amount of neighbouring channels used for normalization
        alpha: multiplicative factor. Default: 0.0001
        beta: exponent. Default: 0.75
        k: additive factor. Default: 1

    Shape:
        - Input: :math:`(N, C, *)`
        - Output: :math:`(N, C, *)` (same shape as input)

    Examples::

        >>> lrn = nn.LocalResponseNorm(2)
        >>> signal_2d = torch.randn(32, 5, 24, 24)
        >>> signal_4d = torch.randn(16, 5, 7, 7, 7, 7)
        >>> output_2d = lrn(signal_2d)
        >>> output_4d = lrn(signal_4d)

